From: mscharged-port
Subject: Leave the debug LAN draft when a peer disconnects
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509
Classification: temporary explicit original-source diagnostic admission

The online lobby exists only in NET_MODE_ONLINE. When a peer is lost during
the captain, sidekick or matchmaking draft, a LAN session is shut down
instead of closing the online lobby's connections (a null dereference), and
the popup returns to Main Menu instead of the online menus. The LAN lobby is
entered without the online camera transition, so the return is a plain Main
Menu push: TransitionOnlineMatchToMainMenu pops a camera this flow never
pushed and crashed from the sidekick draft.

diff --git a/src/Game/SH/SHChooseCaptains.cpp b/src/Game/SH/SHChooseCaptains.cpp
index 371aeb9..d1edd04 100644
--- a/src/Game/SH/SHChooseCaptains.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/SH/SHChooseCaptains.cpp
@@ -1328,6 +1328,15 @@ void ChooseCaptainsSceneV2::OnDisconnectDismissed()
 {
     mPopupActive = false;
     FEAudio::PlayAnimAudioEvent(0x37A9934D, 0, 0, 1);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_LAN)
+    // Not using TransitionOnlineMatchToMainMenu to avoid popping a camera
+    // that was never pushed
+    if (g_pNetworkSessionBase->GetSessionMode() != NET_MODE_ONLINE)
+    {
+        GameSceneManager::Instance()->Push(SCENE_MAIN_MENU, SCREEN_BACK, true);
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     GameSceneManager::Instance()->Push(SCENE_ONLINE_MENU, SCREEN_BACK, true);
 }
 
@@ -1370,7 +1379,14 @@ void ChooseCaptainsSceneV2::SetSelectButtonBounds(int side)
 
 inline void ChooseCaptainsSceneV2::ShowDisconnectedError()
 {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_LAN)
+    if (g_pNetworkSessionBase->GetSessionMode() != NET_MODE_ONLINE)
+        g_pNetworkSessionBase->Shutdown();
+    else
+        g_pNetworkSession->GetOnlineLobby()->CloseConnectionsAndReset();
+#else
     g_pNetworkSession->GetOnlineLobby()->CloseConnectionsAndReset();
+#endif
     NetworkDraft::Instance()->UnregisterMessageReceivers();
     if (GameSceneManager::Instance()->GetSceneType(GameSceneManager::Instance()->GetCurrentScene()) != SCENE_POPUP_MENU)
     {
